-- title:
--   Evaluated Slice Phase Six Seven Reverse Bound
-- statement:
--   **The combined phase-six-to-seven reverse bridge costs at most $4\sqrt{\zeta}$.**
--
--   Let $S$ be a symmetric strategy for parameters $(q,m,d)$ with normalized state, let `family` be a slice-indexed polynomial submeasurement family, and let $\zeta$ be an error scale. Assume both state-dependent squared-distance relations required for the first and second evaluated points hold under the uniform evaluated-slice distribution, each with bound $4\zeta$: the first relation compares the left evaluated point family at $Q_1$ with its total-sandwich family, and the second makes the same comparison at $Q_2$. Then the phase-five and phase-seven endpoints satisfy
--
--   $$
--   \left|
--   \mathbb{E}_Q[\mathrm{evaluatedSlicePhaseFivePaperRemoved}(Q)]
--   -\mathbb{E}_Q[\mathrm{evaluatedSlicePhaseSevenGonnaCite}(Q)]
--   \right|
--   \le 4\sqrt{\zeta}.
--   $$
--
--   The bound is obtained by combining the two $2\sqrt{\zeta}$ reverse-insertion estimates with the triangle inequality. It is the endpoint comparison consumed by `evaluatedSlice_scalar_chain_bound` for the paper lines 99--104.
--
--   Formalization credit: Sirui Lu, Ruixuan Deng, Yanqiao Zhu, and Zhengfeng Ji (arXiv:2609.19814). Mathematical source: Zhengfeng Ji, Anand Natarajan, Thomas Vidick, John Wright, and Henry Yuen (arXiv:2009.12982).
--
--   **Formalization Note.** The source declaration is `MIPStarRE.LDT.Commutativity.evaluatedSlice_phaseSixSeven_reverse_bound`; its Lean statement gives the exact quantifier order and all boundary hypotheses.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/LionSR/MIPStarRE/blob/f382c801026f53a9efc260fdee707cb35e0adb15/MIPStarRE/LDT/Commutativity/ScalarApproximation/PaperChainReverse.lean#L25-L88

